<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Nail yr headline shr, div rises.</title>
<headline>Nail yr headline shr, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre-exceps	    6.86	  vs 5.39</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 4.16	  vs 3.85</p>
<p>Income</p>
<p>    - attrib		  181.02	vs 29.66</p>
<p>    - headline		28.34	 vs 24.19</p>
<p>    Excepional charge     152.68	vs 15.26</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   180.68	vs 42.19</p>
<p>    Tax			 2.13	  vs 3.28</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   8.02	  vs 4.42</p>
<p>    Operating income	39.05	 vs 32.25</p>
<p>Div payable Jan 12</p>
<p>on register Dec 27</p>
<p>Full name: New Africa Investments Ltd (Nail)</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  14.65	 vs 9.90</p>
<p>NOTE - Nail was part of the black empowerment consortium which in August won control of Johnnies Industrial Corp Ltd from Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>Directors said the results from all operations should improve in the forthcoming year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
